      <section id="how" class="public-section" aria-labelledby="how-title">
        <div class="public-section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Made for the person behind the prompts</p><h2 id="how-title">Less digging. More “oh, that’s why.”</h2><p>Start with the overview. Open the exact turn when you want the details.</p></div>
        <div class="public-cards">
          <article><span class="step-number">01</span><h3>Bring the work together</h3><p>Link supported sources to your account. Find conversations, tool calls and received activity by agent, project or session.</p><span class="public-tag">Capture &amp; activity</span></article>
          <article><span class="step-number peach">02</span><h3>Find what needs a look</h3><p>Use built-in signals or create your own. Follow a finding to its evidence and decide whether the rule got it right.</p><span class="public-tag">Signals &amp; evidence</span></article>
          <article><span class="step-number lilac">03</span><h3>Keep useful corrections</h3><p>Save your verdict against the exact captured turn. Those reviewed examples are the foundation for the learning work ahead.</p><span class="public-tag">Review &amp; feedback</span></article>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section id="coverage" class="public-section public-coverage" aria-labelledby="coverage-title">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Connections, without the guessing</p><h2 id="coverage-title">Start where your AI works.</h2><p>A collector runs where the work happens. Its local queue keeps pending records for another delivery attempt when the connection returns.</p><p class="muted">Coverage depends on the source you connect. A subscription alone does not give RROFLOW access to every app or conversation.</p><a class="text-button" data-member-link href="/app#sources">Explore source setup →</a></div>
        <div class="connection-list"><article><strong>Claude Code &amp; Codex</strong><span>Session collectors</span><p>Read supported session files across projects for the linked operating-system user.</p></article><article><strong>Claude, Codex &amp; Grok SDKs</strong><span>Instrumented applications</span><p>Adapters record calls made through them. Compatibility tests use fixture providers; live-provider verification is still ahead.</p></article><article><strong>ChatGPT, Grok &amp; other subscription apps</strong><span>Coverage still being developed</span><p>Browser and mobile history is not automatically connected. Remote work must report from its execution source.</p></article></div>
      </section>
      <section id="learning" class="public-section learning-banner" aria-labelledby="learning-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">The next chapter · being built</p><h2 id="learning-title">Better examples.<br />Better learning.</h2><p>The direction is automatic datasets, supervised learning from corrections, and unsupervised discovery of recurring problems. Proposed changes must be evaluated before promotion and remain reversible.</p></div><ol aria-label="Planned learning loop"><li>Capture evidence</li><li>Review &amp; label</li><li>Build a dataset <small>Planned</small></li><li>Evaluate &amp; improve <small>Planned</small></li></ol></section>
      <section id="membership" class="public-section member-entry" aria-labelledby="member-title"><p class="eyebrow">Your own space to understand the work</p><h2 id="member-title">A workspace that belongs to you.</h2><p>Account sign-in opens an isolated workspace. The member experience is being built alongside capture, signals and review. Free monitoring and paid dataset capabilities are planned; subscriptions and billing are not active yet.</p><a class="button ink" data-member-link href="/app">Go to your workspace →</a><details><summary>What is ready, and what is still ahead?</summary><p>This development build includes activity, signal creation, evidence review and collector delivery reports. Public signup, subscription entitlements and the live Texas deployment still need end-to-end acceptance. Automatic dataset generation and training are not running.</p></details></section>
